  "question": "Solve this cryptarithm:\n\n   AQRQN\n    UIIN\n     RNA\n     JUU\n    RIGU\n   NQNPN\n   IKGJN\n    RGRR\n     RNN\n   NNKGA\n   GPJPN\n    UGKG\n   IQUIN\n   RNAGJ\n    APGP\n    GNKP\n     AJN\n   INKQK\n     UPJ\n   RIIGK\n    GJRI\n     NIK\n     JJP\n     NQI\n+   JPJA\n--------\n  PIKQUR\n\nEach letter stands for a unique digit (0-9). No leading letter can be zero.\nProvide a comma separated mapping from letters to digits that satisfies the equation in your final answer. Output format: \"A=1,B=2,C=3\" (without quotes)\n\nIMPORTANT: When you finish, put ONLY the final answer inside \\boxed{...} (no extra text). If the task requests a multi-line format, encode it into a single line representation.",
