      "thought": "I need to solve a cryptarithm where 26 numbers are added together to form a 6-digit sum. I will write a Python script using a constraint satisfaction approach to find the unique digit (0-9) for each letter (A, Q, R, N, U, I, J, G, P, K).",
      "action": "execute_python",
      "action_input": "{\"code\": \"from itertools import permutations\\n\\ndef solve():\\n    letters = 'AQRNIUJGKP'\\n    # There are 10 unique letters: A, Q, R, N, U, I, J, G, P, K\\n    # Each must be a unique digit 0-9.\\n    \\n    # Numbers list\\n    words = [\\n        'AQRQN', 'UIIN', 'RNA', 'JUU', 'RIGU', 'NQNPN', 'IKGJN', 'RGRR', 'RNN', 'NNKGA',\\n        'GPJPN', 'UGKG', 'IQUIN', 'RNAGJ', 'APGP', 'GNKP', 'AJN', 'INKQK', 'UPJ', 'RIIGK',\\n        'GJRI', 'NIK', 'JJP', 'NQI', 'JPJA'\\n    ]\\n    result_word = 'PIKQUR'\\n    \\n    # Leading letters cannot be zero\\n    leading = set(word[0] for word in words + [result_word])\\n    \\n    indices = {l: i for i, l in enumerate(letters)}\\n    leading_indices = [indices[l] for l in leading]\\n    \\n    for p in permutations(range(10)):\\n        if any(p[i] == 0 for i in leading_indices):\\n            continue\\n        \\n        mapping = {letters[i]: p[i] for i in range(10)}\\n        \\n        def to_num(word):\\n            n = 0\\n            for char in word:\\n                n = n * 10 + mapping[char]\\n            return n\\n        \\n        total_sum = sum(to_num(w) for w in words)\\n        if total_sum == to_num(result_word):\\n            res = ','.join(f\\\"{l}={mapping[l]}\\\" for l in sorted(mapping.keys()))\\n            return res\\n\\nprint(solve())\"}",
